<a id="platform"></a>
<h2>2. Android service boundary</h2>
<p>The host is a FlutterActivity. Commands return a result to their caller. Progress, meter samples and hypotheses use reverse calls on the same channel.</p>
<h3>Channel contract</h3>
<table><thead><tr><th>Caller</th><th>Operation</th><th>Result and ownership</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Flutter</td><td><code>notes</code>, mutations</td><td>The host queries SQLite and returns a list of JSON records. Mutation calls complete after the write. Dart reloads the committed list.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Flutter</td><td><code>present</code>, <code>download</code></td><td>The worker checks local assets or downloads and loads the model. Permission to record is requested separately, when starting capture.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Flutter</td><td><code>record</code>, <code>test</code>, <code>stop</code>, <code>cancel</code></td><td>A successful start acknowledges microphone initialization. Stop requests completion. Its return does not imply inference has finished.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Android</td><td><code>level</code>, <code>partial</code></td><td>RMS and elapsed seconds update the meter. Each partial string replaces the previous preview.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Android</td><td><code>finishing</code>, <code>finished</code>, <code>ended</code></td><td>Finishing begins after the take is durable. Finished carries text and an optional edit target. Ended releases controls after cancellation, silence rejection or an error.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Flutter</td><td><code>import</code>, <code>merge</code></td><td>The picker returns a document URI. The host validates its records and returns a count. User confirmation triggers a transaction that inserts missing IDs.</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>The worker serializes native calls because capture, final flush and abort share a transcriber. UI events return to Android's main thread before crossing the channel. Manual stop and silence detection converge on the same completion path. When final processing is cancelled, the completed audio file remains available to retry.</p>
